From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nico Burns <nico@nicoburns.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:34:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lock trackpad scroll gestures to their main axis

Trackpad swipes are rarely straight, and Blitz applied both deltas of
every wheel event, so a vertical swipe over a horizontal scroller moved
it sideways, and a horizontal swipe on it moved the page a little.

BlitzWheelEvent now carries winit's gesture phase and scroll source.
Each event in a trackpad gesture is locked by a decayed sum of the
gesture's recent movement (as in Chromium): to an axis while recent
movement along it is at least twice the other, and to both while
diagonal, so a gesture that turns unlocks and can lock again. Momentum
scrolling carries on from the finger gesture it follows; physical mouse
wheels and events outside a gesture scroll both axes as before, and
mouse-wheel notches still take 0034's smooth scroll path. Cancelled
wheel events still update the gesture state.

Ported from blitz#1638 (commit bb611089, fixes blitz#1630) onto the
pinned revision, keeping 0034's smooth wheel-notch path and updating
0035's overscroll-behavior test for the new BlitzWheelEvent fields.

Co-authored-by: Jake Cattrall <krazyjakee@gmail.com>
